        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0093" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg21"/>

                <head>No. 16.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    Osborn</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 14,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 13, of the 10th
                    ultimo, and am much pleased to see the evidence of the good will borne by Brazil
                    to the United States which is contained in the imperial government’s prompt
                    acceptance of the invitation to send representatives to an American Congress in
                    November next.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
